<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles VII of France</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1403">1403</a>–<a href="/years/1461">1461</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Charles the Victorious</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles VII was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> from 1422. Helped by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joan-of-arc">Joan of Arc</a>, who raised the siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orleans">Orléans</a> and saw him crowned at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reims">Reims</a> in 1429, he recovered northern France and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gascony">Gascony</a> from the English, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a>. He created a standing army and royal taxes, besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/metz">Metz</a> in 1444 and annexed Comminges to the crown in 1454.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-vii-of-france.jpg" alt="Charles VII of France" width="320" height="390" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:KarlVII.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
